      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143467",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{6}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cBernoulli(\u03b8)$ and unknown probability of success $\u03b8$. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{6}$, you're given that\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(6)x_{i} = 5$.\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a Bernoulli random variable is given by*\n$f(x) = \u03b8^{x}(1 - \u03b8)^{1 - x}, x = 0, 1$."
